Run the OnePlus 6T (fajita) board config on a OnePlus 6 (enchilada) with the 5.10.194 kernel and /data in RAM:
- modules: use the 5.10.194-sdm845 module set + load list instead of 6.6.101 (modules come from scripts/04-build-kernel.sh)
- fstab.fajita: no /data entry (the phone's own userdata stays Android's); init.fajita.cfg mounts a tmpfs on /data
- init.fajita.cfg: the system init.cfg creates /data/service/el0/* and runs load_access_token_id BEFORE this vendor
  pre-init job, i.e. on the read-only root; redo that on the tmpfs, otherwise every native service gets token 0
  (samgr: AddSystemAbilityInner PERMISSION DENIED) and init panics the kernel
- init.fajita.usb.cfg: the dwc3 controller is a600000.dwc3 on 5.10 (a600000.usb is the 6.6 name); hdc needs it
- logdump.sh + service: optional boot-log channel (only with op6.logdump=1 on the kernel command line)

